      "formal_statement": "Formal Name: MeasureTheory.condExp_mul_of_stronglyMeasurable_right | Kind: theorem | Type: ∀ {Ω : Type u_1} {m mΩ : MeasurableSpace Ω} {μ : MeasureTheory.Measure Ω} {f g : Ω → ℝ},\n  MeasureTheory.StronglyMeasurable g →\n    MeasureTheory.Integrable (f * g) μ → MeasureTheory.Integrable f μ → μ[f * g|m] =ᵐ[μ] μ[f|m] * g | Path: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Function.ConditionalExpectation.PullOut",
      "informal_statement": "Let $(\\Omega,\\mathcal{F},\\mu)$ be a measure space and let $m\\le\\mathcal{F}$ be a sub‑σ‑algebra.  Suppose $g\\colon\\Omega\\to\\mathbb{R}$ is $m$‑strongly measurable and $f\\colon\\Omega\\to\\mathbb{R}$ is such that both $f$ and the product $f\\cdot g$ are integrable with respect to $\\mu$.  Then the conditional expectation of the product satisfies\\[\\mathbb{E}_\\mu[f\\,g\\mid m]=\\mathbb{E}_\\mu[f\\mid m]\\cdot g\\quad\\mu\\text{-a.e.}\\]  In other words, the conditional expectation of $f\\,g$ given $m$ equals the product of the conditional expectation of $f$ given $m$ with the factor $g$, almost everywhere with respect to $\\mu$."
