      "informal_statement": "Let $(\\Omega,\\mathcal{F},\\mu)$ be a measure space and let $\\mathcal{G}\\subseteq\\mathcal{F}$ be a sub‑σ‑algebra.  Suppose $f\\colon\\Omega\\to\\mathbb{R}$ is $\\mathcal{G}$‑strongly measurable and $g\\colon\\Omega\\to\\mathbb{R}$ is integrable together with the product $f\\cdot g$.  Then the conditional expectation of the product satisfies\\[\\mathbb{E}_\\mu[f\\,g\\mid\\mathcal{G}]\\;=\\;f\\cdot\\mathbb{E}_\\mu[g\\mid\\mathcal{G}]\\quad\\text{μ-a.e.}\\]  In Lean notation this is written as\\[\\mu[f\\,g\\mid\\mathcal{G}] =ᵐ[\\mu] f \\cdot \\mu[g\\mid\\mathcal{G}].\\]"
