      "informal_statement": "Let $(\\Omega,\\mathcal{F},\\mu)$ be a measure space and let $m\\leq\\mathcal{F}$ be a sub‑σ‑algebra.  Suppose $g\\colon\\Omega\\to\\mathbb{R}$ is $\\mu$‑almost everywhere strongly measurable and that $f\\colon\\Omega\\to\\mathbb{R}$ satisfies \\[\\int_{\\Omega}|f|\\,d\\mu<\\infty\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\\int_{\\Omega}|f\\,g|\\,d\\mu<\\infty\\] (i.e. $f$ and $f\\,g$ are integrable).  Then the conditional expectation of the product $f\\,g$ with respect to $m$ satisfies\\[\\mathbb{E}_\\mu[f\\,g\\mid m]=\\mathbb{E}_\\mu[f\\mid m]\\cdot g\\quad\\mu\\text{-a.e.}\\] In other words, a factor $g$ that is $m$‑almost everywhere strongly measurable can be pulled out of the conditional expectation on the right."
