      "formal_statement": "Formal Name: MeasureTheory.condExp_mul_of_aestronglyMeasurable_left | Kind: theorem | Type: ∀ {Ω : Type u_1} {m mΩ : MeasurableSpace Ω} {μ : MeasureTheory.Measure Ω} {f g : Ω → ℝ},\n  MeasureTheory.AEStronglyMeasurable f μ →\n    MeasureTheory.Integrable (f * g) μ → MeasureTheory.Integrable g μ → μ[f * g|m] =ᵐ[μ] f * μ[g|m] | Path: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Function.ConditionalExpectation.PullOut",
      "informal_statement": "Let $(\\Omega, \\mathcal{F}, \\mu)$ be a measure space and $m \\le \\mathcal{F}$ a sub-\\sigma-algebra. For functions $f,g : \\Omega \\to \\mathbb{R}$, assume $f$ is $\\mu$-almost everywhere strongly measurable, $f\\cdot g$ is $\\mu$-integrable, and $g$ is $\\mu$-integrable. Then\\n\\n\\[\\n\\mathbb{E}_\\mu[f\\cdot g \\mid m] = f \\cdot \\mathbb{E}_\\mu[g \\mid m] \\quad \\mu\\text{-a.e.}\\n\\]"
