      "informal_statement": "Let $(\\Omega,\\mathcal{F},\\mu)$ be a finite measure space and let $m\\leq \\mathcal{F}$ be a sub-$\\sigma$-algebra. Suppose $f:\\Omega\\to\\mathbb{R}$ is $m$-strongly measurable and essentially bounded by a constant $c$, i.e. $\\|f(\\omega)\\|\\leq c$ for $\\mu$-almost every $\\omega$. Let $g:\\Omega\\to\\mathbb{R}$ be integrable. Then the conditional expectation of the product satisfies \\[ \\mathbb{E}_\\mu[f\\,g\\mid m] = f\\,\\mathbb{E}_\\mu[g\\mid m] \\quad \\mu\\text{-a.e.} \\]"
