      "informal_statement": "Let $(\\Omega,\\mathcal{F},\\mu)$ be a finite measure space and let $m\\leq\\mathcal{F}$ be a sub-$\\sigma$‑algebra.  Suppose $f\\colon\\Omega\\to\\mathbb{R}$ is $\\mu$‑almost surely strongly measurable and essentially bounded by a constant $c$, i.e. $\\|f(\\omega)\\|\\le c$ for $\\mu$‑a.e. $\\omega$.  Let $g\\colon\\Omega\\to\\mathbb{R}$ be integrable.  Then the conditional expectation of the product satisfies\\[\\mathbb{E}_\\mu[f\\,g\\mid m]=f\\cdot\\mathbb{E}_\\mu[g\\mid m]\\quad\\mu\\text{-a.e.}\\]"
