      "formal_statement": "Formal Name: MeasureTheory.condExp_stronglyMeasurable_simpleFunc_mul | Kind: theorem | Type: ∀ {Ω : Type u_1} {m mΩ : MeasurableSpace Ω} {μ : MeasureTheory.Measure Ω},\n  m ≤ mΩ →\n    ∀ (f : MeasureTheory.SimpleFunc Ω ℝ) {g : Ω → ℝ}, MeasureTheory.Integrable g μ → μ[⇑f * g|m] =ᵐ[μ] ⇑f * μ[g|m] | Path: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Function.ConditionalExpectation.PullOut",
      "informal_statement": "Let $(\\Omega,\\mathcal{F},\\mu)$ be a measure space and let $m\\leq\\mathcal{F}$ be a sub-\\(\\sigma\\)-algebra.  For any simple function $f\\colon\\Omega\\to\\mathbb{R}$ that is $m$‑measurable (i.e. $m$‑strongly measurable) and any integrable function $g\\colon\\Omega\\to\\mathbb{R}$, the conditional expectation of the product $f\\cdot g$ given $m$ is almost everywhere equal to the product of $f$ with the conditional expectation of $g$ given $m$:\\[\\mathbb{E}_\\mu[f\\cdot g\\mid m]\\;=\\;f\\cdot\\mathbb{E}_\\mu[g\\mid m]\\quad\\mu\\text{-a.e.}\\]  Here $\\mathbb{E}_\\mu[h\\mid m]$ denotes the conditional expectation of a function $h$ with respect to the sub‑$\\sigma$‑algebra $m$."
