      "full_name": "MeasureTheory.condExp_bilin_of_stronglyMeasurable_left",
      "formal_statement": "Formal Name: MeasureTheory.condExp_bilin_of_stronglyMeasurable_left | Kind: theorem | Type: ∀ {Ω : Type u_1} {m mΩ : MeasurableSpace Ω} {μ : MeasureTheory.Measure Ω} {E : Type u_2} {F : Type u_3} {G : Type u_4}\n  [inst : NormedAddCommGroup E] [inst_1 : NormedSpace ℝ E] [inst_2 : NormedAddCommGroup F] [inst_3 : NormedSpace ℝ F]\n  [inst_4 : NormedAddCommGroup G] [inst_5 : NormedSpace ℝ G] [inst_6 : CompleteSpace G] (B : F →L[ℝ] E →L[ℝ] G)\n  [inst_7 : CompleteSpace E] {f : Ω → F} {g : Ω → E},\n  MeasureTheory.StronglyMeasurable f →\n    MeasureTheory.Integrable (fun ω => (B (f ω)) (g ω)) μ →\n      MeasureTheory.Integrable g μ → μ[fun ω => (B (f ω)) (g ω)|m] =ᵐ[μ] fun ω => (B (f ω)) (μ[g|m] ω) | Path: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Function.ConditionalExpectation.PullOut",
      "informal_statement": "Let $(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mu)$ be a measure space and $m\\le\\mathcal F$ a sub‑$\\sigma$‑algebra.  Let $B\\colon F\\to_{\\mathbb R}\\mathcal L(E,G)$ be a continuous bilinear map (i.e. a continuous linear map from $F$ to the space of continuous linear maps $E\\to G$).  Suppose $f\\colon\\Omega\\to F$ is strongly $m$‑measurable and $g\\colon\\Omega\\to E$ is integrable, and that the function $\\omega\\mapsto B(f(\\omega))(g(\\omega))$ is integrable.  Then for $\\mu$‑almost every $\\omega$ we have\\[\\mathbb E_{\\mu}\\bigl[\\,B(f(\\omega))(g(\\omega))\\mid m\\bigr](\\omega)=B\\bigl(f(\\omega)\\bigr)\\bigl(\\mathbb E_{\\mu}[g\\mid m](\\omega)\\bigr).\\]"
