      "informal_statement": "Let $(\\Omega,\\mathcal{F},\\mu)$ be a measure space and let $\\mathcal{m}\\subseteq\\mathcal{F}$ be a sub‑σ–algebra.  Let $E$ be a Banach space over $\\mathbb{R}$ and let\\n\\n- $f:\\Omega\\to\\mathbb{R}$ be $\\mu$‑integrable,\\n- $g:\\Omega\\to E$ be $\\mu$‑integrable and $\\mu$‑almost everywhere strongly measurable.\\n\\nThen the conditional expectation of the pointwise product $f\\cdot g$ with respect to $\\mathcal{m}$ satisfies\\n\\n$$\\mu[f\\cdot g \\mid \\mathcal{m}] \\;=\\; \\mu[f \\mid \\mathcal{m}]\\;\\cdot\\; g \\qquad \\mu\\text{-a.e.}$$\\n\\nHere $f\\cdot g$ denotes the scalar multiplication of the real‑valued function $f$ with the $E$‑valued function $g$, and $\\mu[f\\mid\\mathcal{m}]$ is the conditional expectation of an integrable function with respect to $\\mathcal{m}$.  The equality holds outside a set of $\\mu$‑measure zero."
