      "formal_statement": "Formal Name: MeasureTheory.integral_eq_zero_iff_of_nonneg_ae | Kind: theorem | Type: ∀ {α : Type u_1} {m : MeasurableSpace α} {μ : MeasureTheory.Measure α} {f : α → ℝ},\n  0 ≤ᵐ[μ] f → MeasureTheory.Integrable f μ → (∫ (x : α), f x ∂μ = 0 ↔ f =ᵐ[μ] 0) | Path: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.Bochner.Basic",
      "informal_statement": "For any real-valued function $f \\colon \\alpha \\to \\mathbb{R}$ that is almost everywhere nonnegative with respect to a measure $\\mu$ and is integrable, the Bochner integral of $f$ is zero if and only if $f$ is almost everywhere zero with respect to $\\mu$, i.e.,\n\\[ \\int f \\, d\\mu = 0 \\leftrightarrow f = 0 \\text{ $\\mu$-a.e.} \\]"
