      "informal_statement": "For a measurable set $s$ and a non-negative real-valued function $f$ that is integrable on $s$ with respect to a measure $\\mu$, the integral of $f$ over $s$ is zero if and only if $f$ equals zero almost everywhere on $s$ with respect to the restricted measure $\\mu \\restriction s$."
