      "informal_statement": "Let $a \\leq b$ be real numbers, $f : \\mathbb{R} \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be a function that is nonnegative almost everywhere on the interval $(a, b]$ with respect to a measure $\\mu$, and interval integrable on $[a, b]$. Then the integral of $f$ over $[a, b]$ is zero if and only if $f$ equals zero almost everywhere on $(a, b]$ with respect to $\\mu$, i.e.,\n\\[ \\int_a^b f(x) \\, d\\mu = 0 \\leftrightarrow f = 0 \\text{ $\\mu$-a.e. on } (a, b]. \\]"
