      "informal_statement": "Let $f \\colon \\alpha \\to E$ be an integrable function with respect to a measure $\\mu$. If for every measurable set $s$ with finite measure $\\mu(s) < \\infty$, the integral of $f$ over $s$ is zero, i.e.,\n\\[\n\\int_s f \\, d\\mu = 0,\n\\]\nthen $f$ is equal to zero almost everywhere with respect to $\\mu$, i.e., $f = 0$ $\\mu$-a.e."
